In this case, we can drop the last `m - n` columns of `Q` to form the
**reduced QR decomposition**:

.. math::

    A = QR\mathrlap{\qquad Q \in \mathbb{K}^{m \times n}, R \in \mathbb{K}^{n \times n}}

